course: dictionary
lesson: 7888
title: One word, many meanings: range
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Range is a good example. To find the right one, read the words around it and ask what would fit. «The zoo has a wide range of animals.» Here a range is a set of different things of one kind, so it means a mix of animals.
explain: In maths, the range is the difference between the smallest and the biggest number in a set. Numbers can also range from one value to another: «ages range from 6 to 10» means the ages go from 6 up to 10. The words «from» and «to» are the clues that tell you it means limits.
explain: Range can also mean how far something can reach. «The phone signal was out of range in the valley» means the signal could not reach that far. Look for clues like «out of» or «in» to know which meaning the writer chose.
fact: Range has several meanings, so always check the words around it.
fact: «Range» can mean a set of different things of one kind, as in «a range of colours».
fact: In maths, the range is the biggest number minus the smallest number.
fact: «Ages range from 6 to 11» means the ages go from 6 up to 11.
fact: A range is also a cooker, and a range of hills or mountains is a row of them.
exercise: «The zoo has a wide range of animals.» What does range mean here? | A row of hills | How far something can reach | *A set of different things of one kind | A cooker
exercise: «Ages range from 6 to 10.» What does range from ... to ... mean? | Count backwards | Cook something slowly | Reach very far away | *Go between two limits
exercise: In the numbers 2, 9, 4, 7, what is the range? | *7 | 11 | 5 | 3
test: «The phone signal was out of range in the valley.» What does out of range mean? | Cooked for too long | Full of hills | *Too far away to reach | Very strong and clear
test: «The Rockies are a range of mountains in North America.» What is a range of mountains? | A small, flat field | *A row of mountains | A set of numbers in maths | Dinner cooked on a stove
exam: Mum bought a new range for the kitchen. In this sentence, range means: | A set of different things | A row of hills | How far something can reach | *A cooker
